{{/*
~/.gdbinit — load GEF (GDB Enhanced Features) into every gdb session.

dev_machine + Linux only: this file and the gef.py it sources are gated out on
prod_machine and Windows in .chezmoiignore.tmpl (TARGET paths: .gdbinit,
.config/gdb). gef.py is vendored at chezmoi/dot_config/gdb/gef.py, pinned to GEF
release 2024.06 — the LAST release supporting Python 3.6–3.9 (EL9 gdb embeds
Python 3.9; GEF 2025.01+ needs 3.10 and would SyntaxError on load). Provenance +
the don't-bump-past-2024.06 constraint live in its .vendor sidecar.

This is a .tmpl ONLY to resolve the absolute home dir — gdb's `source` does not
shell-expand `~`, so we emit the full path. GEF is non-destructive: every native
gdb command still works; it just adds the dashboard/context UI.

The OTHER GDB front-end, pwndbg, is installed as a SEPARATE standalone `pwndbg`
command (makefile/lib/pwndbg.sh) and does NOT hook in here — so `gdb` → GEF,
`pwndbg` → pwndbg, and the two never collide. To use vanilla gdb for a session:
`gdb -nx`.
*/ -}}
